<LegalLayout title="Privacy Policy" updated={updated} path="/privacy" description="How Terrarun collects, uses, and protects your data — including location and health data used to track your runs.">
  <p>This Privacy Policy explains how <strong>Terrarun</strong> ("Terrarun", "we", "us", "our") collects, uses, shares, and protects information when you use the Terrarun mobile app and <a href="/">striderunning.run</a> (together, the "Service"). Terrarun is a location-based running game — location is core to how it works, and this Policy is written to be honest about exactly what that means. <strong>We do not sell your personal information.</strong> The free Android app may show ads; iPhone and Terrarun Pro do not.</p>
  <p>By using the Service you agree to this Policy. If you do not agree, please do not use the Service.</p>

  <h2>1. Information we collect</h2>
  <h3>Information you give us</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Account:</strong> email address, username, optional display name, avatar photo, bio, and your chosen territory colour and flag. If you sign in with Apple or Google, we receive the account identifier and the email address that provider shares with us (with Apple you may choose to hide your real email and share a private relay address instead). We never receive or store your Apple or Google password.</li>
    <li><strong>About you (all optional):</strong> gender (used only to pick your in-app body silhouette), date of birth (used to verify you meet the minimum age and to tailor stats), and how often you run. You can decline these.</li>
    <li><strong>Content you create:</strong> posts, comments, photos you attach, kudos, clubs and club cover photos, events, and challenges.</li>
    <li><strong>Safety contacts (optional):</strong> names and contact details of people you choose to add. We store them only so the app can show them to you; we never contact them ourselves or use them for marketing.</li>
    <li><strong>Email enquiries:</strong> if you email us from the website, your email address and the contents of your message.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Information collected as you run</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Precise location (GPS):</strong> we record your route <em>while you actively track a run</em> — including in the background during an active run if you grant background permission — to calculate distance, pace, splits, and the territory you enclose. We do not track your location when you are not viewing the map or recording a run. You can deny location entirely and use the app in explore mode.</li>
    <li><strong>Activity data:</strong> distance, duration, pace, elevation, splits, and captured area for each run.</li>
    <li><strong>Approximate location/city:</strong> derived once, with your permission, to place you on city and country leaderboards and surface nearby events. You can hide yourself from leaderboards in Settings.</li>
    <li><strong>Anti-cheat signals:</strong> we analyse the GPS data of each run (speed profile, accuracy, movement signature) to detect vehicle use and GPS spoofing. This protects the fairness of the game and is applied equally to everyone.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Health data (only if you connect it)</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Apple Health (HealthKit):</strong> if you choose to connect, we read heart rate, active energy (calories), and workouts to show heart-rate zones and effort on your runs, and we write your Terrarun runs to Apple Health as workouts. <strong>HealthKit data is never used for advertising or marketing, is never sold, and is never shared with third parties.</strong> You can disconnect at any time in the app or revoke access in the iOS Health app, and you can ask us to delete any health-derived data we hold.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Collected automatically</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Device &amp; diagnostics:</strong> app version, device model, OS version, crash reports and performance traces (via Sentry) so we can fix problems. The Android build includes Google Mobile Ads; the iPhone build excludes that SDK and does not request the App Tracking Transparency permission.</li>
    <li><strong>Ads on Android:</strong> the free Android tier may show ads from Google AdMob. Where required, Google’s consent flow runs before ads are requested. Depending on your consent choices and region, Google may process device identifiers, approximate location derived from IP, ad interactions and diagnostics to deliver, measure and protect ads. Health data and precise run routes are not provided to AdMob. Pro removes ads.</li>
    <li><strong>Push token:</strong> if you enable notifications, a device push token so we can deliver them. Every notification category can be turned off in Settings.</li>
    <li><strong>Motion (on-device only):</strong> the app may use the accelerometer to animate on-screen effects (for example, liquid that tilts with your phone). This sensor data is processed on your device in real time and is never recorded or transmitted.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>If you subscribe to Terrarun Pro</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Purchases:</strong> Terrarun Pro is an optional auto-renewing subscription. Apple processes purchases made inside the iPhone app. Paddle.com Market Ltd is the merchant of record for purchases made on this website: Paddle collects the payment, tax and billing details and sends the receipt. We never receive or store your full card number or security code. We receive the purchase and entitlement status needed to unlock Pro for your account.</li>
    <li><strong>Paywall provider (Superwall):</strong> we use Superwall to present offers and manage subscriptions. It receives a pseudonymous app-user identifier, your subscription/entitlement status, and basic device and locale information to show the right offer and record the purchase. It does not receive your name, email, runs, location, or health data, and it is not an advertising or cross-app tracking service.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. How we use information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Provide the core game — track your runs, compute and display territory, and run leaderboards, leagues, clubs, events, and challenges.</li>
    <li>Display your profile, posts, and territory to other players (see Section 3 for exactly what is visible).</li>
    <li>Send notifications you have enabled (your turf was taken, a close call, streak reminders, kudos, comments, nearby events).</li>
    <li>Send service and account emails (welcome, security, subscription receipts, and replies to your requests) and — unless you opt out — occasional product emails such as weekly recaps, streak reminders, and re-engagement nudges. Every product email has a one-tap unsubscribe link, and you can manage email preferences at any time; service and security emails are not marketing and are sent regardless.</li>
    <li>Keep the game fair — detect cheating, review flagged runs, and enforce our <a href="/terms/">Terms</a>.</li>
    <li>Keep the Service safe — moderate reported content, action blocks and reports, and prevent abuse.</li>
    <li>Maintain, debug, and improve the Service.</li>
    <li>Comply with law and protect rights and safety.</li>
  </ul>
  <p><strong>Legal bases (EEA/UK):</strong> performance of our contract with you (running the game you signed up for), your consent (location, health data, notifications, optional profile fields — each separately revocable), our legitimate interests (anti-cheat, security, service improvement — balanced against your rights), and legal obligations.</p>

  <h2>3. What other players can see</h2>
  <p>Terrarun is a competitive, social game. By design, other players can see: your username, display name, avatar, tier/level, flag, your territory (its shape, colour, and size in m²), your position on leaderboards, and the posts, comments, clubs, and events you create. Your run posts can include your route map.</p>
  <p><strong>Your controls:</strong> set activity privacy to Everyone, Followers, or Only me; hide yourself from leaderboards; block any user (two-way — they can no longer see or contact you); report any content or user; delete any of your content at any time. Your email, date of birth, gender, health data, and safety contacts are <strong>never</strong> visible to other players.</p>

  <h2>4. How we share information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Service providers</strong> that help operate the Service: Supabase (database, authentication, file storage, realtime infrastructure, and email-delivery functions), Apple and Google (sign-in, when you choose them), Mapbox (map tiles and rendering — receives map viewport requests), Apple and Expo (push notification delivery), Superwall (iPhone subscription presentation and entitlement management), Apple (App Store payment processing), Google AdMob (Android advertising and consent), Resend (transactional and product email delivery), Sentry (crash diagnostics), and Cloudflare (website hosting). Their handling of data is governed by their role and contractual/data-protection terms.</li>
    <li><strong>Paddle:</strong> for website purchases, Paddle.com Market Ltd acts as merchant of record and processes checkout, billing, tax, receipts, subscription status and refunds. Paddle receives the account linkage and billing information needed to complete and support the purchase; it does not receive your run routes or health data from Terrarun.</li>
    <li><strong>Apple Health, if you connect it:</strong> data flows only in the directions described above, on your device, under Apple's HealthKit rules.</li>
    <li><strong>Legal:</strong> if required by law, subpoena, or to protect the rights, property, or safety of Terrarun, our users, or the public.</li>
    <li><strong>Business transfer:</strong> if Terrarun is acquired or merged, your data may transfer to the successor, who must honour this Policy or notify you of changes.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We <strong>do not sell</strong> personal information and we <strong>do not share</strong> it for cross-context behavioural advertising (as those terms are defined in the California Consumer Privacy Act).</p>

  <h2>5. Your rights &amp; choices</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Access, correct, export, delete:</strong> you can edit your profile in-app, and <strong>delete your account and all of its data in-app</strong> (Settings → Delete account) — this permanently removes your profile, runs, territory, posts, and connections. You can also email us for a copy of your data.</li>
    <li><strong>Permissions:</strong> location, notifications, photos, motion, and health access can each be revoked at any time in iOS Settings; the app keeps working with reduced features.</li>
    <li><strong>EEA/UK:</strong> you additionally have the rights of access, rectification, erasure, restriction, portability, and objection, and the right to withdraw consent at any time and to lodge a complaint with your supervisory authority.</li>
    <li><strong>California:</strong> you have the right to know, delete, correct, and to non-discrimination for exercising your rights. We do not sell or share personal information, so there is nothing to opt out of.</li>
    <li><strong>California — sensitive personal information:</strong> precise geolocation, and any health data you connect, are "sensitive personal information" under the CPRA. We use them <strong>only</strong> to provide and secure the features you ask for (tracking your runs, computing territory, showing effort) — never to infer characteristics about you and never for advertising. Because our use is already limited to those purposes, the CPRA right to "limit the use of my sensitive personal information" does not change how we treat it; you can still revoke location or Apple Health access at any time in iOS Settings.</li>
    <li>To exercise any right, email <a href="mailto:privacy@striderunning.run">privacy@striderunning.run</a>. We respond within the time required by your local law (e.g., 30 days under GDPR, 45 days under CCPA) and will verify the request comes from the account holder.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. Data retention</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Account, runs, territory, and content: kept while your account is active.</li>
    <li>Account deletion: removes your data immediately from production; residual copies leave encrypted backups within their normal rotation period (up to ~30 days).</li>
    <li>Territory history may be retained in <strong>anonymised, aggregate</strong> form (no longer linked to you) for game-integrity statistics.</li>
    <li>Crash diagnostics are retained per Sentry's rolling window (90 days or less).</li>
    <li>Disconnecting Apple Health stops all health reads immediately; you can also revoke access in the iOS Health app.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>7. Security</h2>
  <p>We use industry-standard safeguards: encryption in transit (TLS) for all traffic, database row-level security so each account can only reach its own private data, and least-privilege access. No method of transmission or storage is 100% secure; if a breach affecting your personal data occurs, we will notify you and the relevant authorities as required by law.</p>

  <h2>8. Children</h2>
  <p>Terrarun is not directed to children under 13 (or the higher minimum age your country sets for consent to data processing — e.g., up to 16 in parts of the EEA), and we do not knowingly collect their data. The app asks for your date of birth and refuses sign-up below the minimum age. If you believe a child has provided us data, contact us at <a href="mailto:privacy@striderunning.run">privacy@striderunning.run</a> and we will delete it promptly.</p>

  <h2>9. International transfers</h2>
  <p>Your information may be processed in countries other than your own, including the United States, where our service providers operate. Where required, we rely on appropriate safeguards such as the EU Standard Contractual Clauses and our processors' equivalent commitments.</p>

  <h2>10. Changes to this Policy</h2>
  <p>We will update this Policy as the Service evolves and revise the "Last updated" date above. For material changes we will notify you in-app or by email before they take effect. The current version always lives at <a href="https://striderunning.run/privacy">striderunning.run/privacy</a> — the app links directly to this page (Settings → Privacy Policy and at sign-up).</p>

  <h2>11. Contact</h2>
  <p>Privacy questions or requests: <a href="mailto:privacy@striderunning.run">privacy@striderunning.run</a><br/>General support: <a href="mailto:support@striderunning.run">support@striderunning.run</a></p>
</LegalLayout>
